We disagree slightly. If you're optimizing your game, using the ?ea to
rustproof once everything is +4 or +5 is proper.  I rarely bother
unless I'm already in a closet enchanting other stuff--in practice,
once I'm already at AC -35 or lower, it's not going to significantly
affect my ascension chances.  But if you're playing more
conservatively, it certainly is the right thing to do.

Which doesn't seem far from what Rast wrote: "If you have extra ?EA,
you might as well use them, but it won't change the eventual outcome
of your game." (I disagree theoretically with the last clause, but not
much practically)



